  "question": {
    "text": "A straight line through the point A(3, 4) is such that its intercept between the axes is bisected at A. Its equation is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XqNyC",
      "text": "\nx + y = 7\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wKAti",
      "text": "\n3x − 4y + 7 = 0\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fHU5M",
      "text": "\n4x + 3y = 24\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "7HzVU",
      "text": "\n3x + 4y = 25",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The equation of axes is $x y=0$\n$\\Rightarrow$ the equation of the line is $\\frac{x \\cdot 4+y \\cdot 3}{2}=12 \\Rightarrow 4 x+3 y=24$",
    "image": null
  },
